Lay-What: The weekly box restart can now restart a desktop machine that has someone logged in, when that machine is set to allow it.
Lay-How: It asks the system itself to restart, which stops every program cleanly, instead of asking the login manager, which said no.
Lay-Why: The planned restart of a desktop machine failed twice, so the machine kept running past its weekly restart.
